NOTE ON CONFLICT: An earlier version of my brief said "no React/TypeScript/Bootstrap/jQuery". That is SUPERSEDED. The final decision is: use ALL of the technologies above, but SELECTIVELY and without conflicts, as defined below.

Role of each technology:
- Astro: project structure, layouts, file-based routing, static generation (SSG), components. Use Astro's official integrations (@astrojs/react, @astrojs/sitemap, Tailwind via its currently officially supported setup). Do not use deprecated APIs. Use current stable, mutually compatible versions and follow each package's official setup instructions.
- HTML5: semantic landmarks (header, nav, main, section, article, aside, footer).
- Tailwind CSS: responsive utility styling and layout, wired to the design tokens (theme config).
