8. STRICT FORM VALIDATION (ALL FORMS)
====================================================================
Applies to: contact, newsletter (home banner + footer), login, signup, quiz, checkout, coupon, quantity, search/filter inputs where relevant, and any other form.

Build ONE reusable validation module (src/lib/validation.ts) used by Astro scripts, React islands and jQuery code alike, exporting pure functions: validateName, validateEmail, validatePassword, validatePhone, validateRequired, validateQuantity, validateCoupon, validateSelect, validateTextarea. Each returns { valid, message }.

A. Required: trim before validating; reject empty and whitespace-only; show a clear message next to each invalid field; no success state until ALL pass.
B. Name: reusable function + regex, reject digits, reject empty/whitespace-only, support international names (Unicode letters and marks), spaces, hyphens, apostrophes (straight and curly). Starting pattern (apply after trim, requires Unicode property escapes support, verify the build target supports it): /^[\p{L}\p{M}]+(?:[ '\u2019-][\p{L}\p{M}]+)*$/u. Names like "John2", "A1ice", "12345" must be rejected; "Jean-Luc", "O'Brien", "María José", "Zoë", "محمد علي" accepted.
C. Email: reusable function + practical pattern, reject empty, malformed, missing local part, missing domain, whitespace inside, bad dot placement (leading/trailing/consecutive dots), no TLD. Combine type="email" with JS validation. Do not claim the mailbox exists.
D. Password (demo): clear requirements text, validated minimum length (e.g. 8+) and at least basic complexity as documented, confirmation must match, show/hide toggle works, never log/expose password values, no real authentication.
E. Phone (if present): trim; accept international formats with + ( ) - . spaces; require a reasonable digit count (e.g. 7–15 digits); reject letters/malformed; no single-country pattern.
F. Others: required selects, quantity is positive integer within bounds, required quiz answer, coupon per documented demo rules, checkout fields, textarea min length after trim.
G. Behavior: errors next to fields; aria-invalid and aria-describedby; focus the first invalid field on submit; accessible error summary for longer forms (checkout, signup); not color-alone (icon/text); clear errors as the user corrects; prevent duplicate submission while processing (disabled button + loading state); success only after validation passes; never a false success. Use native attributes (required, type, minlength, maxlength, autocomplete, inputmode) plus JS validation (use noValidate on the form and custom messages so UX is consistent, while keeping native semantics).

